  "body": "The `HTMLTableColElement` interface is defined in section 4.9.3 for the `colgroup` element. That section includes a definition of the [`span`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#dom-colgroup-span) IDL attribute:\r\n\r\n> The **span** IDL attribute must [reflect](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/common-dom-interfaces.html#reflect) the content attribute of the same name. It is [clamped to the range](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/common-dom-interfaces.html#clamped-to-the-range) [1, 1000], and its default value is 1.\r\n\r\nThe exact same prose appears at [the end of section 4.9.4](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#dom-col-span) for the `col` element, which re-uses the `HTMLTableColElement` interface. This creates two exported definitions of the `span` IDL attribute for `HTMLTableColElement`. I think the second definition should rather be a reference to the first. Or perhaps the second text could be dropped altogether since 4.9.3 already describes the behavior of the `span` IDL attribute?",
